WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:03.467
♪♪

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.534
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:07.834
Okay, so in the credits
last week, we...

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.400
had a credit that said
the show was produced

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.968
by the O'Reilly Crime Syndicate.

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:16.767
That was, of course,
a reference to the family

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:20.033
that is really running things
here in the building.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:25.300
I know O'Reilly is not
their real last name...

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:33.133
...but I have used
their real last name

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:33.968
in the past,

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:37.133
and when I did...

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:40.334
I was told in no uncertain terms

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.601
[Irish accent] to never use
the real name, boyo.

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:46.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:47.634
[ Normal voice ]
And I was not told politely.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.601
Let me make clear.

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.834
Walking down the hallway
after a show,

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:56.267
all of a sudden
the lights go off...

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:58.467
bag over my head.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:03.467
And I knew it was them, because
there were like 20 of them.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:07.434
It's like 40...rough hands
giving me the business.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:12.801
The message was received
is all I'm saying.

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:15.434
You might be wondering,
"Oh, Seth, you have security.

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:16.267
Where it was John?"

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:19.033
Where was John...O'Malley?

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:24.901
Would you believe he had
a "family emergency" that day?

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.701
Pretty convenient.

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.200
[ Clears throat ]

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.767
We showed
this Amelia Earhart statue

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:39.434
from Purdue University.

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:40.968
You can see the name there.
This actually --

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:43.234
Someone at Purdue said

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:45.901
it's actually
right outside Earhart Hall.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.300
It's a residence hall.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.667
I guess
it's one of the nicest ones.

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.133
Only problem -- hard to find.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:57.934
I said it was
a little troubling

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.834
they made a statue of her where

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:03.801
she's holding a very important
part of the plane.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.234
But I guess this was a --
this is a famous moment,

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:09.367
one of her favorite --
one of her famous quips.

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:12.634
She was also known --

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:17.300
She is known as
"the Oscar Wilde of the skies."

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:21.300
And she was walking
by holding this.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.434
Legend goes...

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.367
Someone said,
"Hey, Amelia, don't you

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:28.467
need that for your plane?"

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:29.634
And she said, "Oh, this?

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:31.300
No, this is just a prop."

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:42.100
We talked about
how the MGM lion roar

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.767
is actually a tiger roar

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:46.634
because the tiger
sounds fierce in a way

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:51.200
we, the audience,
expect a lion to sound.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.801
A jackal reached out to say
not only that,

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:55.467
when you hear an eagle scream

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:57.868
in a commercial, film,
television,

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:02.801
they're actually using
the sound of a red-tailed hawk.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.634
I looked this up.
I confirmed this.

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:10.200
Because an actual bald eagle
sounds like a squeegee.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.334
So I was curious to hear
what that would sound like.

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:16.601
Let's take a listen.

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.734
-[ As Andrew Squiggman ]
Hello!

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.434
-Oh, a Squiggy.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.934
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.567
I read that --

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.400
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.534
I read that one wrong.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:37.567
Let's just get through the --
my worst part of the week.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:40.434
I have said --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.567
I have said time and time
and time again,

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:48.734
don't use the P.O. box to send
me Mac Tonight merchandise.

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:49.834
Okay?

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:52.701
It's like the one thing
I don't want.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.267
And it keeps showing up.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.467
Actually, it's not.
I want to reiterate.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:57.868
It's not
the one thing I don't want.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.267
There's two things
I want you to send me --

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:01.367
Mac Tonight merchandise

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.167
and Fabergé eggs.

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:06.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.968
So I'm going to show you
this week's haul

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.901
in a reverse order
of how distressing I found it.

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:20.601
I don't -- I don't care for this
jacked blue guy at all.

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:22.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.601
I don't -- This looks like...

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.868
looks like he'd have his way
with you.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:29.868
Um, this -- Look.

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:31.834
This is impressive
craftsmanship,

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:35.133
but this isn't a piece of rock
art I know what to do with.

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.767
I don't care for the fact

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.934
that it's holding
in a mug that says

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:40.767
Wally down by its crotch.

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:47.934
Again, I appreciate the time --

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:50.000
I don't like
when you make it me.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.000
I don't like that.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:53.868
That's worse.

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.901
It's worse when it's me.

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:01.501
And I know a lot of you think
to overcome my fears,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.000
I have to become them.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.701
Or at least I guess that's
the message of this nightmare.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:14.834
And then...this came.

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:17.868
It's like Happy Meal toys,
right?

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:19.400
And you might be like,

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.234
"Hey, Seth,
that seems less distressing

00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:23.734
than everything else
you've show me."

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:25.801
Well, here's the thing,
you guys.

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:28.167
it came
with this card that says,

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:31.167
"Congratulations
on your new home."

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:36.534
Like, I guess implying
they [bleep] know where I live?

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:39.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:47.000
It's like Mac
from [bleep] "Watcher."

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:53.734
[ Sighs ]

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:57.534
I was sent one other
Mac Tonight-themed thing,

00:05:57.534 --> 00:06:03.434
and it is, no exaggeration, too
distressing to show on TV...

00:06:04.834 --> 00:06:06.567
...and I know it is
too distressing

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:10.734
because I showed it
to someone at NBC Standards,

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:14.767
and exactly a week after I
showed it to them, they died.

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:17.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.133
And they know it was
Mac Tonight related,

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:24.033
because they did an autopsy

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:26.267
and they died from
an overdose...

00:06:26.267 --> 00:06:27.501
of Filet-O-Fish.

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:31.467
They had two.

00:06:31.467 --> 00:06:33.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:36.701
And you might be like,
"Seth, you saw it.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:39.067
Obviously, you had to see it
before you showed it

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:40.601
to the person
at NBC Standards.

00:06:40.601 --> 00:06:41.634
Like, how come you didn't die?"

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:43.601
I feel terrible to say this.

00:06:43.601 --> 00:06:46.200
I think I lived because
I showed it to someone else.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:50.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:54.100
So, if you ever see it
for a quarter of a second...

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.834
make sure you show it
to someone else.

00:06:59.067 --> 00:07:01.067
Um...

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:03.167
Bathrooms don't echo.
They reverberate.

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:05.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:07.834
Um...

00:07:10.367 --> 00:07:13.267
Echoes gets smaller
with each successive one.

00:07:13.267 --> 00:07:15.234
I guess when I did my echo,
I didn't get quieter.

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.167
So to the person who said that,
I just want to say

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:19.634
you're annoying, you're
annoying, you're annoying...

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:21.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:24.267
Um, Marjorie Taylor Greene
couldn't kick open

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:25.934
a bathroom door like a saloon

00:07:25.934 --> 00:07:27.067
because they only open in.

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:28.567
Don't count her out.

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:30.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.968 --> 00:07:35.601
George Santos lied about playing
volleyball at Baruch College.

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:40.567
I said Baruch College
isn't exactly renowned

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:42.868
for its volleyball program.

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:44.567
One of you took offense
and said --

00:07:44.567 --> 00:07:47.033
and these are their words --

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:50.100
"Baruch College has won
their league pretty regularly

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:53.000
and had some moderate
post-season success."

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.767
So I stand corrected.

00:08:00.767 --> 00:08:03.033
What I should have said
was Baruch College

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:05.567
isn't exactly renowned
for its volleyball program.

00:08:05.567 --> 00:08:08.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.701
We talked about Biden
maybe having secret documents

00:08:14.701 --> 00:08:16.968
from his time in the Senate,
which started in 1973.

00:08:16.968 --> 00:08:18.868
We joked that
he would be listening

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:20.634
to classified 8-track cassettes.

00:08:20.634 --> 00:08:23.067
We referenced Blue Oyster Cult's

00:08:23.067 --> 00:08:26.334
"(Don't Fear) The Reaper."

00:08:26.334 --> 00:08:29.634
Well, a bunch of
Blue Oyster Cult superfans,

00:08:29.634 --> 00:08:32.167
otherwise known
as the Blue Oyster Cult...

00:08:32.167 --> 00:08:34.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.234 --> 00:08:40.701
...they reached out to say
that song was from 1976,

00:08:40.701 --> 00:08:43.734
and Biden, again, as we
established, started in 1973.

00:08:43.734 --> 00:08:45.334
I kind of thought
it was within the realm

00:08:45.334 --> 00:08:46.634
that it didn't have
to be the first year,

00:08:46.634 --> 00:08:48.968
but I guess I should
have dug harder...

00:08:48.968 --> 00:08:51.334
found a song from 1973.

00:08:51.334 --> 00:08:52.968
So, if you want to take this

00:08:52.968 --> 00:08:55.200
and you can edit it
into that "Closer Look" for

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.133
when you go back to watch it...

00:08:57.133 --> 00:08:59.367
since you're so [bleep] upset
about it...

00:08:59.367 --> 00:09:02.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.334 --> 00:09:03.934
"Ah, this...

00:09:03.934 --> 00:09:07.968
Leroy Brown guys sounds bad.

00:09:07.968 --> 00:09:09.934
'Bad' bad."

00:09:09.934 --> 00:09:13.701
[ Laughter ]

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:16.200
We showed our favorite video
that we often show --

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.100
Joe Biden
tripping up the stairs.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:21.367
And our joke was if you showed
that video -- because, again,

00:09:21.367 --> 00:09:23.000
we're taking note
of the fact

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.467
that it's so hard to figure out
how you can trip up --

00:09:25.467 --> 00:09:27.033
if you showed that video
to Isaac Newton,

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:29.000
he'd burn up his notebooks
and start over.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.400
Some of you said
it would be more likely

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:31.968
that if we showed that video
to Isaac Newton,

00:09:31.968 --> 00:09:35.000
he would freak out
over video technology.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.901
You might think, but all he
cared about was gravity.

00:09:40.701 --> 00:09:42.868
It didn't matter
how it was packaged,

00:09:42.868 --> 00:09:44.501
he just focused on the gravity.

00:09:44.501 --> 00:09:48.567
If a naked woman fell from
the sky and landed in his lap,

00:09:48.567 --> 00:09:51.434
all he would care about
was that she came straight down.

00:09:54.167 --> 00:09:58.334
You know, he was not liked...

00:09:58.334 --> 00:10:01.701
by the mathematicians
of his era...

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:04.801
because they also knew
the whole time

00:10:04.801 --> 00:10:08.234
that if an apple fell,
it would fall down.

00:10:08.234 --> 00:10:11.133
And they didn't realize
that if they told somebody that

00:10:11.133 --> 00:10:13.167
they'd be known
as the father of gravity.

00:10:13.167 --> 00:10:15.467
[ Laughter ]

00:10:17.434 --> 00:10:19.634
So he was formally known
as Sir Isaac Newton,

00:10:19.634 --> 00:10:23.167
but to them, they called him --
behind his back, of course --

00:10:23.167 --> 00:10:24.667
No [bleep] Newton.

00:10:24.667 --> 00:10:28.467
[ Laughter ]

00:10:30.801 --> 00:10:32.634
I guess a couple of weeks ago

00:10:32.634 --> 00:10:35.634
we talked about
Norwegian tourists

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:39.901
in Times Square looking
for the M&amp;M's store, and...

00:10:39.901 --> 00:10:42.367
well...

00:10:42.367 --> 00:10:45.400
someone from Norway
took offense at...

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.767
the grammar we claimed
Norwegians would have

00:10:48.767 --> 00:10:49.767
if they were speaking English.

00:10:49.767 --> 00:10:51.267
"Dear Seth, you had a bit

00:10:51.267 --> 00:10:52.901
where you did
a Norwegian impression,

00:10:52.901 --> 00:10:53.834
and it was disappointing.

00:10:53.834 --> 00:10:55.734
I think you missed the accent,

00:10:55.734 --> 00:10:57.801
but more troubling
was the grammar.

00:10:57.801 --> 00:10:59.934
Even those Norwegians
with heavy accents

00:10:59.934 --> 00:11:02.400
are likely to be very
comfortable with the language.

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:06.534
Consider Jens Stoltenberg,
sexy General Secretary --

00:11:06.534 --> 00:11:08.501
Secretary, sorry,
General of NATO

00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:10.701
and former
Prime Minister of Norway

00:11:10.701 --> 00:11:12.367
as a possible example.

00:11:12.367 --> 00:11:14.901
Thank to you
for be reading this.

00:11:14.901 --> 00:11:18.033
May up be the place.
You keep the good work."

00:11:18.033 --> 00:11:19.400
So, it fell apart at the end.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.868
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.734 --> 00:11:29.367
We showed a video
last "Corrections"

00:11:29.367 --> 00:11:32.033
proving that when the Roadrunner
says "meep, meep"

00:11:32.033 --> 00:11:33.200
it's not the noise it's making,

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:37.701
it's the WB censors
meeping them out.

00:11:37.701 --> 00:11:40.000
And we got our hands
on an uncensored version,

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.133
and we showed that when

00:11:41.133 --> 00:11:43.133
the "meep, meep,"
you hear it on screen,

00:11:43.133 --> 00:11:45.267
what the Roadrunner was actually
saying was "[bleep] off."

00:11:45.267 --> 00:11:47.701
And a bunch of you asked,
"Why would the 'off' be meeped?

00:11:47.701 --> 00:11:48.767
Why wouldn't it be 'meep off'?"

00:11:48.767 --> 00:11:50.400
Well, you obviously
don't have kids

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.133
because if it's "meep, meep,"
you can tell the kids

00:11:52.133 --> 00:11:53.501
that's the sound
the Roadrunner's making.

00:11:53.501 --> 00:11:55.300
If it's "meep off,"
then they want to know

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.601
what the meep is for, right?

00:11:56.601 --> 00:11:57.634
And then the whole day,
they're like,

00:11:57.634 --> 00:11:59.133
"What's the meep?
What's the meep?"

00:11:59.133 --> 00:12:00.834
And you're like, "It's not
for you. It's only for adults."

00:12:00.834 --> 00:12:02.367
And they're like, "We want to
know! We want to know!"

00:12:02.367 --> 00:12:04.400
And then eventually you hit
your breaking point

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:05.534
and you tell them
to [bleep] off.

00:12:05.534 --> 00:12:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:12:11.334 --> 00:12:14.434
Someone wrote, "In real life,
coyotes catch and eat

00:12:14.434 --> 00:12:16.067
roadrunners all the time."

00:12:18.234 --> 00:12:19.200
Cool.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.300
[ Laughter ]

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.033
Pass that on to my friends
at "Looney Tunes."

00:12:26.033 --> 00:12:30.300
[ Laughter ]

00:12:35.868 --> 00:12:39.801
I said
someone knit me this jackal,

00:12:39.801 --> 00:12:42.200
when it is clearly "cro-cheted."

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.234
[ Laughter ]

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.501
[ Laughter ]

00:12:50.501 --> 00:12:52.234
Uh, complaint.

00:12:52.234 --> 00:12:54.767
Not a correction,
a complaint...

00:12:54.767 --> 00:12:57.167
that I've stopped doing
my Al Pacino impression.

00:12:57.167 --> 00:12:58.334
And it's true.

00:12:58.334 --> 00:13:00.701
There was a time
when I was doing it

00:13:00.701 --> 00:13:03.267
with great regularity,
but that time has passed.

00:13:06.267 --> 00:13:08.901
I think of my impressions...

00:13:08.901 --> 00:13:11.701
not as voices I'm doing...

00:13:13.601 --> 00:13:17.734
...but rather tiny people
who are inside me,

00:13:17.734 --> 00:13:20.133
using me as a vessel
to tell their stories.

00:13:22.434 --> 00:13:23.701
And when they've told
their stories,

00:13:23.701 --> 00:13:27.167
I think it is best to move on

00:13:27.167 --> 00:13:31.501
so it doesn't hinder
my own personal growth.

00:13:31.501 --> 00:13:35.767
So with my Pacino,
as much as it pained me...

00:13:35.767 --> 00:13:38.367
to do so...

00:13:38.367 --> 00:13:40.601
it was time...

00:13:40.601 --> 00:13:42.267
to say goodbye
to my little friend.

00:13:42.267 --> 00:13:45.901
[ Laughter ]

00:13:54.734 --> 00:13:56.501
Someone wrote, "Correction --
you don't give penicillin

00:13:56.501 --> 00:13:57.934
for gonorrhea,

00:13:57.934 --> 00:14:02.534
but they do usually
give one dose of ceftriaxone."

00:14:02.534 --> 00:14:05.167
And that one was sent
to us by...

00:14:05.167 --> 00:14:06.400
anonymous.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.667
[ Laughter ]

00:14:14.834 --> 00:14:17.300
Let's see.
Is there anything else?

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:19.467
-[ Shrieking ]
-Seven days!

00:14:19.467 --> 00:14:23.567
[ Laughter ]

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.934
I feel very confident
that this will be

00:14:32.934 --> 00:14:35.334
our most watched "Corrections."

00:14:35.334 --> 00:14:37.234
[ Laughter ]

00:14:37.234 --> 00:14:40.100
Or else there are going to be
a lot of dead jackals!

00:14:42.434 --> 00:14:43.968
See me next week!

